{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LD3dhceBg3Sz5qjaPvAe4o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n5\t- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n6\t\n7\t## Paper Type\n8\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n11\t\n12\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n13\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n14\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n15\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n16\t\n17\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n18\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n19\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n20\t\n21\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n22\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n23\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n24\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n25\t\n26\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n27\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n28\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n29\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n30\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation (exploratory)**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33). **DEMOTED to exploratory** per Dream #6 three-tier consensus: N=33, CI wide [−0.71, −0.16], not strong enough for numbered contribution. This evidence is suggestive but should NOT appear in abstract/conclusion as core support.\n31\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n32\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227). plan_020 circularity ablation is the second pillar. GSM1K correlation (plan_004 Step 3) is supplementary/exploratory only.\n33\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n34\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n35\t\n36\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n37\t\n38\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n39\t\n40\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n41\t\n42\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n43\t\n44\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n45\t\n46\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n47\t\n48\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n49\t\n50\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens + actionable protocol**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. **Actionable contribution**: DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers (monitoring frequency, decision rules, response options).\n51\t\n52\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF serves as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations, with a concrete audit protocol for benchmark maintenance.\"\n53\t\n54\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n55\t\n56\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n57\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n58\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n59\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n60\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n61\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n62\t- §6 Conclusion\n63\t\n64\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n65\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n66\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n67\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n68\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n69\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n70\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n71\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n72\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n73\t\n74\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n75\t\n76\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n77\t\n78\t## Venue Fit\n79\t\n80\t- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n81\t\n82\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n83\t\n84\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n85\t\n86\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n87\t\n88\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n89\t\n90\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n91\t\n92\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n93\t\n94\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n95\t\n96\t1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n97\t\n98\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n99\t\n100\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n101\t\n102\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n103\t\n104\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). **plan_028 in progress**: checking METABENCH for ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA response matrices to run multi-benchmark temporal DIF. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work if METABENCH lacks other benchmarks.\n105\t\n106\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n107\t\n108\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n109\t\n110\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n111\t\n112\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n113\t\n114\t10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n115\t\n116\t11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n117\t\n118\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n119\t\n120\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n121\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n122\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n123\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02a66d51-3ac6-408a-bb4a-e92f7256c0c6","uuid":"87dfd7ad-fa37-4486-b3c7-7d5e329e6cf5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:50:27.576Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122440/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation (exploratory)**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33). **DEMOTED to exploratory** per Dream #6 three-tier consensus: N=33, CI wide [−0.71, −0.16], not strong enough for numbered contribution. This evidence is suggestive but should NOT appear in abstract/conclusion as core support.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227). plan_020 circularity ablation is the second pillar. GSM1K correlation (plan_004 Step 3) is supplementary/exploratory only.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens + actionable protocol**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. **Actionable contribution**: DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers (monitoring frequency, decision rules, response options).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF serves as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations, with a concrete audit protocol for benchmark maintenance.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). **plan_028 in progress**: checking METABENCH for ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA response matrices to run multi-benchmark temporal DIF. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work if METABENCH lacks other benchmarks.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n\n10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n\n11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PPPX6qiQD3TR9j1GCbEwbc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"METABENCH MMLU 5219×12508 response matrix MH-DIF 全量分析：temporal/ability cohort、within-family confound control、domain-specificity\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_cohort\": {\n7\t        \"n_ref_2023\": 1080,\n8\t        \"n_foc_2024h1\": 807,\n9\t        \"ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n10\t        \"ets_b_pct\": 18.2,\n11\t        \"ets_a_pct\": 50.5,\n12\t        \"n_c_items\": 3918,\n13\t        \"mean_abs_delta_mh_c_items\": 2.31\n14\t      },\n15\t      \"ability_cohort\": {\n16\t        \"ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n17\t        \"enrichment\": 1.19\n18\t      },\n19\t      \"within_family\": {\n20\t        \"llama2_vs_llama3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n21\t        \"mistral_vs_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7\n22\t      },\n23\t      \"domain_specificity\": {\n24\t        \"spearman_rho_c_pct_vs_acc_delta\": 0.307,\n25\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n26\t        \"highest_c_pct_subject\": \"moral_scenarios (48.4%)\",\n27\t        \"lowest_c_pct_subject\": \"college_biology (20.7%)\",\n28\t        \"unweighted_mean_c_pct\": 30.0\n29\t      },\n30\t      \"sanity_checks\": {\n31\t        \"random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n32\t        \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n33\t      },\n34\t      \"li_et_al_proxy\": {\n35\t        \"coverage\": 0.738,\n36\t        \"enrichment_temporal\": 0.96,\n37\t        \"fpr_on_li_clean\": 0.318\n38\t      }\n39\t    },\n40\t    \"tables\": [\n41\t      \"Table 1: Temporal DIF summary — N_ref=1080, N_foc=807, %A/B/C by ETS class, mean |Δ_MH|\",\n42\t      \"Table 2: 57-subject domain-specificity — per-subject C%, accuracy delta, sorted descending\",\n43\t      \"Table S1: Within-family DIF — Llama-2v3 (N=161 vs 308), Mistral-Mixtral, C%, Jaccard with temporal\"\n44\t    ],\n45\t    \"figures\": [],\n46\t    \"analysis\": \"31.3% 是 paper 的 anchor number。Random split 0.18% 建立了 chance baseline（plan_029 permutation null 将进一步强化）。Ability cohort 的 2.9% 排除了 ability grouping 作为 confound。Domain ρ=0.307 说明 \\\"模型在某些 domain 进步更多\\\" 是 factor 之一，但不是主要因素——item-level decomposition (plan_019/030) 证明 DIF 主要是 item-specific。Within-family Llama-2→3 的 61.3% 提供了 capability evolution 的 direct evidence，同时为 plan_027 ability confound 分析铺垫。\\n\\n\\n31.3% C% 反映 genuine temporal item-level functioning changes。三层确认非伪影： (1) random split 仅 0.18%（>170x enrichment ratio 排除统计伪影）； (2) ability cohort C%=2.9%（DIF 由 temporal structure 驱动，非 ability grouping）； (3) temporal-ability Jaccard=0.014（两种 cohort 几乎 flag 完全不同的 items）。 Domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation；后续 plan_019 item-level decomposition 证明 domain improvement 仅解释 7.6%。Within-family Llama-2→3 的 61.3% 反映跨代 capability jump（d=-0.99, plan_027），而非 contamination artifact—— 同一架构族内 item functioning 剧烈变化说明 capability evolution 是 contributor 之一。 Li et al. enrichment≈0.96 在 meta-critique framing 下是 expected：web-overlap 是 model-agnostic label，DIF 检测的是 model-cohort-differential signal，二者正交。\\n\"\n47\t  },\n48\t  {\n49\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n50\t    \"description\": \"DIF 对 alignment-RL 和 reasoning-RL 模型的鲁棒性验证，含 per-model detector 对比和 power analysis\",\n51\t    \"results\": {\n52\t      \"alignment_rl_cohort\": {\n53\t        \"n_dpo_orpo_models\": 477,\n54\t        \"temporal_c_pct_with_alignment_rl\": 30.8,\n55\t        \"jaccard_vs_full_temporal\": 0.87,\n56\t        \"dif_retention_ratio\": 0.94\n57\t      },\n58\t      \"reasoning_rl_addition\": {\n59\t        \"n_reasoning_rl_models\": 13,\n60\t        \"models_tested\": \"DeepSeek-R1-7B, DeepSeek-R1-32B, Qwen2.5-RL-7B/14B/32B, Eurus-RL-7B, PRIME-RL-7B, SimpleRL-7B, DAPO-7B, K1.5-RL, TinyZero-3B, DeepScaleR-1.5B, OpenChat-RL\",\n61\t        \"temporal_c_pct_with_rl_added\": 31.1,\n62\t        \"jaccard_vs_full_temporal\": 0.93,\n63\t        \"c_pct_delta_from_baseline\": -0.2\n64\t      },\n65\t      \"per_model_detectors\": {\n66\t        \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.71,\n67\t        \"constat_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.67,\n68\t        \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.43,\n69\t        \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.64,\n70\t        \"mink_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.59,\n71\t        \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.37,\n72\t        \"delong_p_constat_sft_vs_reasoning_rl\": 0.008,\n73\t        \"delong_p_mink_sft_vs_reasoning_rl\": 0.003\n74\t      },\n75\t      \"power_analysis\": {\n76\t        \"exploitation_rate_04_tpr\": 0.28,\n77\t        \"exploitation_rate_06_tpr\": 0.47,\n78\t        \"exploitation_rate_08_tpr\": 0.65,\n79\t        \"exploitation_rate_10_tpr\": 0.79\n80\t      },\n81\t      \"tost_equivalence\": {\n82\t        \"tost_p\": 0.034,\n83\t        \"equivalence_margin\": 0.05,\n84\t        \"ci_90_retention_ratio\": [\n85\t          0.89,\n86\t          0.98\n87\t        ]\n88\t      }\n89\t    },\n90\t    \"tables\": [\n91\t      \"Table S2: Per-model detector AUROC — SFT vs alignment-RL vs reasoning-RL，含 bootstrap 95% CI 和 DeLong test\",\n92\t      \"Table S3: DIF flag stability across cohort compositions — Jaccard, overlap %, new/lost flags\"\n93\t    ],\n94\t    \"figures\": [],\n95\t    \"analysis\": \"Two-level validation 结论清晰：(1) group-level DIF robust to RL composition（Jaccard≥0.87）； (2) per-model detectors fragile to reasoning RL（AUROC drops 0.25-0.27 points）。 这支持 DIF 的 structural advantage 叙事但 N=13 不足以做 standalone claim。 结论：appendix + limitations，为 future work 留出空间。\\n\\n\\nAlignment RL (DPO/ORPO) 不使用 PPO clipping，NLL 分布不变，DIF 不受影响（Jaccard=0.87）。 0.87 而非 1.0 的原因是 alignment RL 模型在 borderline items 上的 response probability 略有 shift，导致少量 items 在 MH threshold 边缘翻转。13 个 reasoning-RL 模型仅占 focal cohort 1.6%， 加入后 C% 几乎不变（31.1% vs 31.3%），因为 MH 是 group-level 统计量——少量个体对 N=807 的 odds ratio 影响可忽略。传统 per-model detectors 在 reasoning-RL 上 AUROC 大幅下降（ConStat 0.71→0.43, Min-K% 0.64→0.37），因为 GRPO/PPO 训练 contracts NLL gaps（Wang et al. 机制），而 DIF 的 group-level conditioning 天然免疫此问题。但 N=13 使 TOST p=0.034 仅 marginal significant， bootstrap CI 宽（[0.89, 0.98]）。Best tier 处理：direction consistent，但诚实地在 limitations 中报告 N=13 underpowered，不作为 numbered contribution。\\n\"\n96\t  },\n97\t  {\n98\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n99\t    \"description\": \"ConStat 风格 perturbation testing——250 MMLU items 的语义等价重述 + 检测 power 评估\",\n100\t    \"results\": {\n101\t      \"reformulation\": {\n102\t        \"n_items_reformulated\": 250,\n103\t        \"semantic_similarity_mean\": 0.92,\n104\t        \"n_models_tested\": 50\n105\t      },\n106\t      \"detection\": {\n107\t        \"constat_flagged_pct_non_rl\": 19.2,\n108\t        \"constat_flagged_pct_all\": 17.8,\n109\t        \"fdr_corrected_flagged_pct\": 12.3\n110\t      },\n111\t      \"comparison_with_dif\": {\n112\t        \"jaccard_constat_vs_dif_c\": 0.24,\n113\t        \"overlap_pct\": 38.2,\n114\t        \"constat_only_pct\": 8.1,\n115\t        \"dif_only_pct\": 22.4\n116\t      },\n117\t      \"power_on_semi_synthetic_gt\": {\n118\t        \"constat_auroc\": 0.68,\n119\t        \"dif_auroc\": 0.82\n120\t      }\n121\t    },\n122\t    \"tables\": [\n123\t      \"Table S4: ConStat detection — flagged % by model class，含 FDR correction\",\n124\t      \"Table S5: DIF × ConStat cross-tabulation — Jaccard, Phi, overlap\"\n125\t    ],\n126\t    \"figures\": [],\n127\t    \"analysis\": \"ConStat 提供 complementary signal 但 Jaccard=0.24 说明 ensemble marginal gain 有限。 Detection mechanism 差异（temporal differential vs memorization sensitivity）使两种方法 检测近乎正交的 item 子集。此结果验证 pivot：DIF 作为 diagnostic lens 的独特价值不可被 ConStat 替代，ensemble 不如 DIF alone + robustness checks 有效。\\n\\n\\nConStat 检测 reformulation sensitivity——contaminated 模型对 verbatim 题回答正确但对 rephrased 版性能下降。19.2% 低于 DIF 31.3%，因为：(1) ConStat 仅覆盖 verbatim memorization，partial/variant contamination 不敏感；(2) MMLU 4-choice format 下 reformulation 的 accuracy drop 天然受限 （chance level 25% 提供 floor）；(3) 高质量 paraphrase 的 surface form 变化可能不足以触发 memorization-dependent 模型的 performance shift。Jaccard=0.24 confirms 两种方法检测不同 signal types——DIF 是 temporal differential functioning，ConStat 是 memorization-specific sensitivity。Semi-synthetic ground truth 上 DIF AUROC 更高（0.82 vs 0.68），因为 injected contamination 是 differential exploitation（与 DIF 检测机制对齐），而非 verbatim memorization （与 ConStat 对齐）。结论：complementary but not additive，验证了 ensemble pivot 的正确性。\\n\"\n128\t  },\n129\t  {\n130\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n131\t    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance 评估——12 open-weight models × 50 responses per item 的 variance-based 检测\",\n132\t    \"results\": {\n133\t      \"setup\": {\n134\t        \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n135\t        \"n_responses_per_item\": 50,\n136\t        \"temperature\": 0.8,\n137\t        \"total_inferences\": 7512000,\n138\t        \"gpu_hours\": 69.6\n139\t      },\n140\t      \"detection\": {\n141\t        \"bimodal_items_pct\": 11.8,\n142\t        \"high_variance_items_pct\": 15.3,\n143\t        \"dvd_flagged_pct\": 13.2\n144\t      },\n145\t      \"comparison_with_dif\": {\n146\t        \"jaccard_dvd_vs_dif_c\": 0.16,\n147\t        \"overlap_pct\": 29.4\n148\t      },\n149\t      \"power\": {\n150\t        \"dvd_auroc_verbatim_gt\": 0.61,\n151\t        \"dvd_auroc_variant_gt\": 0.53\n152\t      }\n153\t    },\n154\t    \"tables\": [\n155\t      \"Table S6: DVD detection — bimodal %, flagged % by model\",\n156\t      \"Table S7: DVD vs DIF cross-tabulation\"\n157\t    ],\n158\t    \"figures\": [],\n159\t    \"analysis\": \"DVD 单独使用 power 不足，且需要 ~70 GPU hours + open-weight access。 Jaccard=0.16 说明 ensemble 增益极小。结果验证了 ensemble pivot 正确性： 三种方法的 detection mechanisms 过于异质，无法有效融合。\\n\\n\\nDVD 依赖 contaminated items 产生 bimodal generation distribution（memorized answer vs random）。 11.8% bimodal 低于 DIF 31.3%，因为：(1) bimodality 仅在 extreme verbatim memorization 下出现， partial exploitation 产生 unimodal 但 shifted distribution；(2) MMLU 4-choice format 的 discrete nature 限制了 generation variance 的 discriminative range——even uncontaminated items 在 temperature sampling 下产生 high variance；(3) requires open-weight access，排除 proprietary models。Jaccard=0.16 极低，confirms DVD 和 DIF 检测几乎完全不同的 item subsets。 AUROC 对比：DVD verbatim 0.61（moderate），variant 0.53（near chance）。Variant contamination detection 接近 chance 因为 paraphrased memorization 不产生 bimodal pattern。\\n\"\n160\t  },\n161\t  {\n162\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n163\t    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合：majority voting + weighted fusion\",\n164\t    \"results\": {\n165\t      \"majority_voting_2of3\": {\n166\t        \"tpr\": 0.35,\n167\t        \"fpr\": 0.08,\n168\t        \"f1\": 0.38\n169\t      },\n170\t      \"weighted_fusion\": {\n171\t        \"optimal_weights\": {\n172\t          \"dif\": 0.58,\n173\t          \"constat\": 0.27,\n174\t          \"dvd\": 0.15\n175\t        },\n176\t        \"tpr\": 0.43,\n177\t        \"fpr\": 0.09,\n178\t        \"f1\": 0.43,\n179\t        \"cross_val_weight_cv\": 0.34\n180\t      },\n181\t      \"dif_alone_reference\": {\n182\t        \"tpr\": 0.51,\n183\t        \"fpr\": 0.31\n184\t      },\n185\t      \"coverage_gain_over_dif_pp\": 4.2,\n186\t      \"all_ensemble_fpr_below_010\": true\n187\t    },\n188\t    \"tables\": [\n189\t      \"Table S8: Ensemble configs — 2-of-3, weighted, DIF-alone，含 95% CI\"\n190\t    ],\n191\t    \"figures\": [],\n192\t    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble 核心问题是三种方法的 signal incommensurability 而非 signal complementarity。 Best tier 下此 negative result 加强了 pivot 叙事：DIF 的 diagnostic lens 价值在于其 独特的 temporal-differential perspective，不需要也不应与其他 mechanism 融合。 Goes to appendix as informative negative result。\\n\\n\\n2-of-3 majority voting TPR 仅 0.35，因为 pairwise Jaccard 0.16-0.24 导致三方法 consensus items 极少——三种方法各自检测不同 signal（temporal differential, memorization sensitivity, generation bimodality），overlap 不足以构建有效 consensus。Weighted fusion 略好（TPR=0.43） 但 cross-validation weight stability 差（CV=0.34），因为 calibration set 有限（semi-synthetic ground truth 200 items）且三种方法 error profiles 不 correlated。DIF alone TPR=0.51 高于 任何 ensemble configuration，因为 high-recall 方法被 ensemble consensus requirement 削弱。 Coverage gain 仅 +4.2pp 不 justify 额外 150 GPU hours 和 open-weight 依赖。\\n\"\n193\t  },\n194\t  {\n195\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n196\t    \"description\": \"GSM8K DIF 复制 + semi-synthetic 验证 + GSM1K contamination gap 相关\",\n197\t    \"results\": {\n198\t      \"step1_temporal_dif\": {\n199\t        \"n_items\": 1319,\n200\t        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n201\t        \"n_foc\": 804,\n202\t        \"standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n203\t        \"external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n204\t        \"sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n205\t        \"standard_external_spearman\": 0.926\n206\t      },\n207\t      \"step2_semi_synthetic\": {\n208\t        \"standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n209\t        \"external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n210\t        \"standard_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508\n211\t      },\n212\t      \"step3_gsm1k_correlation\": {\n213\t        \"n_models\": 33,\n214\t        \"pearson_r\": -0.478,\n215\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.005,\n216\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n217\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n218\t        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n219\t        \"partial_p\": 0.027,\n220\t        \"permutation_p\": 0.014,\n221\t        \"direction\": \"NEGATIVE — opposite to contamination hypothesis\",\n222\t        \"leave_one_out_r_range\": [\n223\t          -0.537,\n224\t          -0.374\n225\t        ]\n226\t      }\n227\t    },\n228\t    \"tables\": [\n229\t      \"Table 4: GSM8K temporal DIF — C% with standard/external matching, random control\",\n230\t      \"Table S9: GSM1K correlation — Pearson/Spearman/partial r，含 leave-one-out robustness\"\n231\t    ],\n232\t    \"figures\": [],\n233\t    \"analysis\": \"GSM8K 复制验证 framework portability（ΔTPR=+0.818）和 temporal DIF pattern（18.9% vs random 0.3%）。 GSM1K negative correlation 在 best tier 下 demote to appendix exploratory（N=33, CI wide）。 This result doesn't weaken any claim — it strengthens the meta-critique by empirically demonstrating DIF and contamination labels capture different signals。\\n\\n\\nGSM8K temporal C%=18.9% 低于 MMLU 31.3%，因为 GSM8K 是 single math domain（1,319 items）， item 功能相对 homogeneous，temporal change 集中在特定难度段而非 broad capability shift。 Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818 高于 MMLU 0.674，因为 GSM8K 更 unidimensional（单一 math 能力维度）， MH 的 unidimensional conditioning 更 appropriate，injection 更 cleanly detected。 GSM1K correlation r=-0.478 方向 opposite to contamination hypothesis：DIF 更多 flag 的模型 有更小的 GSM8K-GSM1K gap。这并不矛盾——DIF flags items whose difficulty changed across cohorts （78% favor 2024），而 small GSM8K-GSM1K gap 的模型恰恰是 genuine capability improvement 最强的（GSM1K 也难，real ability gains transfer）。This anti-correlation 实际上加强了 Claim 2 meta-critique：DIF 和 contamination ground truth 测量的是 different constructs。\\n\"\n234\t  },\n235\t  {\n236\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n237\t    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT equating pilot——验证 MMLU 上 psychometric equating 可行性\",\n238\t    \"results\": {\n239\t      \"model_fit\": {\n240\t        \"unidimensional_rmsea\": 0.121,\n241\t        \"unidimensional_cfi\": 0.776,\n242\t        \"bifactor_5group_rmsea\": 0.094,\n243\t        \"bifactor_5group_cfi\": 0.841,\n244\t        \"bifactor_full_57_convergence\": false,\n245\t        \"bifactor_full_57_error\": \"non-positive definite Hessian after 500 EM iterations\"\n246\t      },\n247\t      \"anchor_selection\": {\n248\t        \"dif_free_items_pct\": 17.3,\n249\t        \"n_anchors_meeting_criteria\": 2163,\n250\t        \"anchor_icc_concordance\": 0.82\n251\t      },\n252\t      \"equating_attempt\": {\n253\t        \"equated_rho\": 0.91,\n254\t        \"target_rho\": 0.95,\n255\t        \"shortfall\": 0.04\n256\t      },\n257\t      \"decision\": \"KILLED — bifactor fit insufficient (RMSEA=0.094>0.05), equated rho=0.91 < target 0.95\"\n258\t    },\n259\t    \"tables\": [\n260\t      \"Table S10: IRT fit comparison — unidimensional vs 5-group bifactor vs full bifactor\"\n261\t    ],\n262\t    \"figures\": [],\n263\t    \"analysis\": \"Informative negative result。说明传统 psychometric equating 不能直接迁移到 LLM multi-domain benchmarks：extreme multidimensionality violates essential unidimensionality assumption。 加强 diagnostic lens framing——DIF 的价值不在于 equating-based item replacement， 而在于 understanding what changed。在 limitations 中自然 motivate future multidimensional IRT。\\n\\n\\nMMLU 57-subject 结构使 full bifactor（1 general + 57 specific）在计算上不可行—— non-positive definite Hessian 因为 57 specific factors 导致 identification 问题（many subjects 仅 100 items，insufficient for factor estimation）。Reduced 5-group bifactor 改善有限 （RMSEA 0.121→0.094, CFI 0.776→0.841），仍远低于 acceptable fit thresholds。根本原因是 MMLU 内在 multidimensionality：从 abstract_algebra 到 world_religions 的 57 domains 无法 被 1 general factor + few group factors 充分 capture。Equating pilot 在 suboptimal fit 下 仍尝试：anchors 数量足够（2,163 items），但 misspecified ability estimates 传播到 fixed-parameter calibration，导致 equated rho=0.91 低于 target 0.95。Kill decision 正确—— 此 negative result 在 limitations 中作为 future multidimensional IRT work 的 motivation。\\n\"\n264\t  },\n265\t  {\n266\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n267\t    \"description\": \"DIF-flagged MMLU items 的 LLM-based 替代 item 生成与难度校准\",\n268\t    \"results\": {\n269\t      \"generation\": {\n270\t        \"n_items_generated\": 400,\n271\t        \"n_subjects\": 10,\n272\t        \"construct_adherence_human_eval\": 0.784\n273\t      },\n274\t      \"difficulty_calibration\": {\n275\t        \"prompt_based_rho\": 0.38,\n276\t        \"student_sim_rho\": 0.52,\n277\t        \"target_rho\": 0.75\n278\t      },\n279\t      \"quality\": {\n280\t        \"human_quality_score_mean\": 3.2,\n281\t        \"human_quality_target\": 4.0,\n282\t        \"holdout_panel_rho\": 0.48\n283\t      },\n284\t      \"decision\": \"BELOW BENCHMARKS — best difficulty rho=0.52 vs target 0.75\"\n285\t    },\n286\t    \"tables\": [\n287\t      \"Table S11: Difficulty calibration — prompt vs student-sim vs empirical，含 95% CI\"\n288\t    ],\n289\t    \"figures\": [],\n290\t    \"analysis\": \"有价值的 negative result——说明 \\\"just regenerate flagged items\\\" 不是 trivial solution。 加强 diagnostic lens framing：DIF 的 actionable value 是 audit protocol + informed maintenance， 而非 automated regeneration。在 Discussion 中可用于回应 reviewer 的 \\\"so what do we do?\\\" question。\\n\\n\\nDifficulty calibration 是 item generation 的瓶颈。Prompt-based targeting（直接指定 difficulty level） rho=0.38，因为 LLM 对 \\\"difficulty for other LLMs\\\" 的 internal calibration 与 empirical difficulty 几乎无关——difficulty 由 knowledge coverage, reasoning depth, distractor quality 联合决定， 非 LLM 自身 uncertainty 可预测。Student simulation 改善到 rho=0.52，但 arXiv 2601.09953 的 r=0.75-0.82 是在 human exam items 上报告的，LLM benchmark items 的 difficulty determinants 不同（e.g., MMLU 多选的 distractor 设计对 LLM 和 human 的 difficulty contribution 不同）。 Construct fidelity 78.4% 说明 22% 的 generated items 有 subject drift 或 cognitive level 错误。 Plan_005 被 kill 后，本 plan 失去 equating framework 支撑。\\n\"\n291\t  },\n292\t  {\n293\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n294\t    \"description\": \"Sinharay et al. (2006) cumulative Bayesian DIF priors 的 4-administration simulation\",\n295\t    \"results\": {\n296\t      \"setup\": {\n297\t        \"n_administrations\": 4,\n298\t        \"n_items_per_sim\": 500,\n299\t        \"n_models_per_admin\": 200,\n300\t        \"true_dif_items\": 100,\n301\t        \"delta_range\": [\n302\t          0.8,\n303\t          1.8\n304\t        ]\n305\t      },\n306\t      \"power_accumulation\": {\n307\t        \"tpr_admin1_d10\": 0.41,\n308\t        \"tpr_admin2_d10\": 0.58,\n309\t        \"tpr_admin3_d10\": 0.72,\n310\t        \"tpr_admin4_d10\": 0.81,\n311\t        \"tpr_admin1_d08\": 0.22,\n312\t        \"tpr_admin2_d08\": 0.38,\n313\t        \"tpr_admin3_d08\": 0.53,\n314\t        \"tpr_admin4_d08\": 0.65\n315\t      },\n316\t      \"fpr_stability\": {\n317\t        \"fpr_range\": [\n318\t          0.042,\n319\t          0.045\n320\t        ]\n321\t      },\n322\t      \"bayesian_shrinkage\": {\n323\t        \"posterior_sd_admin4\": 0.31\n324\t      }\n325\t    },\n326\t    \"tables\": [\n327\t      \"Table S12: Cumulative power — TPR at δ=0.8/1.0/1.4/1.8 × 1-4 administrations\"\n328\t    ],\n329\t    \"figures\": [],\n330\t    \"analysis\": \"Clean simulation 支持 audit protocol 的 operational recommendation：每 6 月 DIF assessment， 3 次累积后 medium effects 的 power 从 0.41 升至 0.72。Goes to appendix，在 Discussion 中 referenced。\\n\\n\\nBayesian evidence accumulation 的 power gain 等价于 effectively increasing sample precision。 δ=1.0 时单次 TPR=0.41（与 phase2 sim 的 N=80 结果一致），4 次累积达 0.81——posterior SD 从 1.0 shrink 到 0.31，precision quadruples。对 small effects（δ=0.8），MH 单次几乎无法检测 （TPR=0.22），但 4 次累积达 0.65——这是 monitoring protocol 的核心理论支撑。 FPR 稳定在 ~0.043 因为 Bayesian shrinkage 对 null items 同样有效（posterior for null items 集中在 0 附近）。Simulation-only 但为 audit protocol 的 monitoring frequency 建议提供 quantitative basis。\\n\"\n331\t  },\n332\t  {\n333\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n334\t    \"description\": \"Benchmark validity 在 progressive item removal 下的降级分析\",\n335\t    \"results\": {\n336\t      \"progressive_removal\": {\n337\t        \"pct_5\": {\n338\t          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9998,\n339\t          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.993,\n340\t          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.98\n341\t        },\n342\t        \"pct_10\": {\n343\t          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9994,\n344\t          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.991,\n345\t          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.96\n346\t        },\n347\t        \"pct_20\": {\n348\t          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9987,\n349\t          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.987,\n350\t          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.92\n351\t        },\n352\t        \"pct_31\": {\n353\t          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9965,\n354\t          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.982,\n355\t          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.87\n356\t        },\n357\t        \"pct_50\": {\n358\t          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9912,\n359\t          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.971,\n360\t          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.78\n361\t        }\n362\t      },\n363\t      \"theoretical_match\": {\n364\t        \"spearman_brown_predicted_rho_31pct\": 0.9968,\n365\t        \"empirical_rho_31pct\": 0.9965,\n366\t        \"gap\": 0.0003\n367\t      }\n368\t    },\n369\t    \"tables\": [\n370\t      \"Table S13: Progressive degradation — rho, reliability, coverage at 5/10/20/31/50%\"\n371\t    ],\n372\t    \"figures\": [],\n373\t    \"analysis\": \"直接支持 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" 叙事。31% instability 不威胁 validity（rho=0.997） 因为 MMLU 的 massive redundancy。Headline number 进 main text，full curve 进 appendix。\\n\\n\\nMMLU 12,508 items 的 massive redundancy 决定了 removal 的 graceful degradation。 Spearman-Brown formula 预测 test length 缩减 31% 时 rho 从 ~1.0 降至 0.9968—— empirical 0.9965 精确匹配，说明 degradation 完全由 test shortening 驱动，无 systematic bias（DIF items 不是 systematically more informative for ranking）。Construct coverage 降速快于 ranking stability，因为 DIF items 在 domains 间非均匀分布（moral_scenarios 48.4% vs college_biology 20.7%），high-DIF domains 在 removal 后 coverage 受损更大。 与 plan_017 实际结果（rho=0.997 at 31%）高度一致。\\n\"\n374\t  },\n375\t  {\n376\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n377\t    \"description\": \"Item-Focused Trees（Tutz & Berger 2016）——连续时间 DIF 作为 MH categorical split 的 robustness check\",\n378\t    \"results\": {\n379\t      \"detection\": {\n380\t        \"ift_flagged_pct\": 28.7,\n381\t        \"jaccard_ift_vs_mh_c\": 0.78,\n382\t        \"ift_only_pct\": 4.2,\n383\t        \"mh_only_pct\": 6.8\n384\t      },\n385\t      \"temporal_patterns\": {\n386\t        \"single_changepoint_pct\": 71,\n387\t        \"multiple_changepoints_pct\": 12,\n388\t        \"gradual_drift_pct\": 17,\n389\t        \"median_changepoint\": \"2023-09\"\n390\t      },\n391\t      \"tree_structure\": {\n392\t        \"mean_terminal_nodes\": 5.2,\n393\t        \"max_depth\": 3\n394\t      }\n395\t    },\n396\t    \"tables\": [\n397\t      \"Table S14: IFT vs MH concordance — Jaccard, overlap, unique flags\",\n398\t      \"Table S15: Changepoint timing distribution by quarter\"\n399\t    ],\n400\t    \"figures\": [],\n401\t    \"analysis\": \"Confirms MH categorical split robustness（Jaccard=0.78）。Changepoint timing 提供 temporal granularity，在 Discussion 中简要引用。Appendix robustness check。\\n\\n\\nIFT 用 continuous release date 替代 MH 的 binary temporal split，避免 arbitrary cutoff。 28.7% vs MH 31.3% 的差异来自 tree-based multiple testing correction（node-level significance threshold）vs MH 的 per-item testing。Jaccard=0.78 高一致性说明 MH categorical split captures the main temporal signal。IFT 的独特 value 是 changepoint timing：71% items 有 single changepoint（median 2023-09，对应 Llama-2/Mistral/Phi-1 release 密集期）， 12% 有 multiple changepoints（progressive drift），17% gradual drift。Timing information 支持 Discussion 中的 \\\"what drives instability\\\" narrative——major model releases 是 item functioning change 的 primary driver。\\n\"\n402\t  },\n403\t  {\n404\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n405\t    \"description\": \"Architecture-homogeneous subpopulation DIF——验证 architecture heterogeneity 非 confound\",\n406\t    \"results\": {\n407\t      \"metabench_composition\": {\n408\t        \"total_models\": 5227,\n409\t        \"decoder_only\": 5226,\n410\t        \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n411\t        \"non_decoder\": 1,\n412\t        \"non_decoder_id\": \"flan-ul2\"\n413\t      },\n414\t      \"dif_comparison\": {\n415\t        \"decoder_only_c_pct\": 31.3,\n416\t        \"full_c_pct\": 31.3,\n417\t        \"jaccard\": 1.0,\n418\t        \"items_changed\": 0\n419\t      },\n420\t      \"irt_fit\": {\n421\t        \"full_rmsea\": 0.121,\n422\t        \"decoder_only_rmsea\": 0.121,\n423\t        \"delta_rmsea\": 0.0\n424\t      }\n425\t    },\n426\t    \"tables\": [\n427\t      \"Table S16: Architecture composition\"\n428\t    ],\n429\t    \"figures\": [],\n430\t    \"analysis\": \"One-line main text defense。IRT misfit 重定向至 limitations（multidimensionality motivation）。\\n\\n\\nMETABENCH MMLU 的 architecture homogeneity 使本实验成为 trivial pass：99.98% decoder-only， 唯一的 encoder-decoder (flan-ul2) 在 N=5227 中的影响可忽略。Jaccard=1.0 意味着 zero items 的 DIF classification 因 architecture stratification 而改变。IRT fit 同样不变 （RMSEA=0.121），因为 misfit 源自 57-subject multidimensionality 而非 architecture heterogeneity。 这是 ideal robustness result：potential confound 被 data composition 自然消除。\\n\"\n431\t  },\n432\t  {\n433\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n434\t    \"description\": \"Known contamination injection 进 real response matrix + DIF detection power 评估 + cross-subject matching 验证\",\n435\t    \"results\": {\n436\t      \"temporal_external_matching\": {\n437\t        \"baseline_fpr\": 0.314,\n438\t        \"tpr_p00\": 0.326,\n439\t        \"tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n440\t        \"tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n441\t        \"tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n442\t        \"tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n443\t        \"delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n444\t        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674\n445\t      },\n446\t      \"ability_external_matching\": {\n447\t        \"baseline_fpr\": 0.493,\n448\t        \"tpr_p10\": 0.8,\n449\t        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302\n450\t      },\n451\t      \"matching_variable_contamination\": {\n452\t        \"standard_fpr_p10\": 0.616,\n453\t        \"standard_fpr_baseline\": 0.298,\n454\t        \"fpr_inflation\": 0.318,\n455\t        \"cross_subject_fpr_inflation\": 0.0\n456\t      },\n457\t      \"cross_subject_5subj_validation\": {\n458\t        \"delta_fpr_all_subjects\": 0.0,\n459\t        \"avg_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n460\t        \"subjects_passing_p05\": \"4/5\"\n461\t      }\n462\t    },\n463\t    \"tables\": [\n464\t      \"Table 5: Semi-synthetic ΔTPR/ΔFPR across exploitation rates and matching strategies\",\n465\t      \"Table 6: Standard vs cross-subject matching FPR comparison\"\n466\t    ],\n467\t    \"figures\": [],\n468\t    \"analysis\": \"ΔTPR=+0.508 是 Claim 3 headline。Cross-subject ΔFPR=0.000 是 key methodological novelty。 Dose-response pattern 提供 internal validity。Both metrics 在 best tier range 内。\\n\\n\\nSemi-synthetic injection 在 real response matrix 上创造 controlled ground truth—— 对 focal cohort 的 known-clean items 执行 incorrect→correct flipping with probability p。 ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 在 best tier [0.45, 0.55] range 内，confirms DIF detects moderate differential contamination。Dose-response（p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0 对应 TPR 0.55→0.83→0.99→1.0） 增强因果推断。关键 methodological finding：standard MH matching（total score 含 contaminated items） 导致 FPR inflation +0.318（matching variable contamination），而 cross-subject matching （other subjects 的 total score）完全消除 inflation（ΔFPR=0.000）。Cross-subject matching works 因为 contamination 是 subject-specific（inject 进特定 subject），而 other subjects 的 total score 不受 contamination 影响，保持 conditioning variable 的 exchangeability。\\n\"\n469\t  },\n470\t  {\n471\t    \"name\": \"multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\",\n472\t    \"description\": \"6 benchmarks temporal DIF——cross-benchmark generalizability 验证\",\n473\t    \"results\": {\n474\t      \"mmlu\": {\n475\t        \"n_items\": 12508,\n476\t        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n477\t        \"n_foc\": 807,\n478\t        \"pct_c\": 31.3,\n479\t        \"random_pct_c\": 0.18\n480\t      },\n481\t      \"winogrande\": {\n482\t        \"n_items\": 1267,\n483\t        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n484\t        \"n_foc\": 803,\n485\t        \"pct_c\": 30.3,\n486\t        \"random_pct_c\": 0.32\n487\t      },\n488\t      \"truthfulqa\": {\n489\t        \"n_items\": 817,\n490\t        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n491\t        \"n_foc\": 807,\n492\t        \"pct_c\": 29.7,\n493\t        \"random_pct_c\": 0.37\n494\t      },\n495\t      \"arc\": {\n496\t        \"n_items\": 1172,\n497\t        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n498\t        \"n_foc\": 807,\n499\t        \"pct_c\": 26.9,\n500\t        \"random_pct_c\": 0.6\n501\t      },\n502\t      \"gsm8k\": {\n503\t        \"n_items\": 1319,\n504\t        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n505\t        \"n_foc\": 804,\n506\t        \"pct_c\": 18.9,\n507\t        \"random_pct_c\": 0.3\n508\t      },\n509\t      \"hellaswag\": {\n510\t        \"n_items\": 10042,\n511\t        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n512\t        \"n_foc\": 807,\n513\t        \"pct_c\": 17.9,\n514\t        \"random_pct_c\": 0.28\n515\t      },\n516\t      \"summary\": {\n517\t        \"range\": \"17.9–31.3%\",\n518\t        \"all_random_below_1pct\": true,\n519\t        \"min_enrichment_ratio\": 44.8,\n520\t        \"mean_c_pct\": 25.8,\n521\t        \"n_benchmarks\": 6\n522\t      }\n523\t    },\n524\t    \"tables\": [\n525\t      \"Table 3: Cross-benchmark temporal DIF — 6 rows, N_items/N_ref/N_foc/C%/random%\"\n526\t    ],\n527\t    \"figures\": [],\n528\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark consistency 是 Claim 1 generalizability 最强证据。17.9-31.3% range 在 best tier [17.0, 32.0] 内。Claim 1 statement 可升级为 \\\"17.9-31.3% across 6 major benchmarks\\\"。\\n\\n\\n6 benchmarks 一致显示 temporal DIF 远超 chance（enrichment 45-174×），确认 temporal item instability 是 LLM benchmark 的 general phenomenon。C% ordering 反映 benchmark 结构： MMLU（57 domains, maximal multidimensionality）和 WinoGrande（commonsense reasoning, capability-sensitive） 最高；HellaSwag（sentence completion, more pattern-matching than reasoning）和 GSM8K （single math domain）最低。低 C% benchmarks 的 items 功能更 homogeneous across model generations ——sentence completion patterns evolve less than knowledge/reasoning items。 All random controls <1% 排除 statistical artifact across all benchmarks。\\n\"\n529\t  },\n530\t  {\n531\t    \"name\": \"permutation_null_c_rate\",\n532\t    \"description\": \"1000× permutation test——temporal label shuffling 下的 C% null distribution\",\n533\t    \"results\": {\n534\t      \"null_distribution\": {\n535\t        \"n_permutations\": 1000,\n536\t        \"mean_c_pct\": 0.21,\n537\t        \"sd_c_pct\": 0.11,\n538\t        \"median_c_pct\": 0.19,\n539\t        \"q95_c_pct\": 0.42,\n540\t        \"q99_c_pct\": 0.54,\n541\t        \"max_c_pct\": 0.71\n542\t      },\n543\t      \"significance\": {\n544\t        \"observed_c_pct\": 31.3,\n545\t        \"z_score\": 282.6,\n546\t        \"empirical_p\": \"<0.001 (0/1000 exceed observed)\",\n547\t        \"ratio_observed_to_null_mean\": 149\n548\t      },\n549\t      \"consistency\": {\n550\t        \"random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n551\t        \"permutation_null_mean\": 0.21,\n552\t        \"convergent\": true\n553\t      }\n554\t    },\n555\t    \"tables\": [\n556\t      \"Table 7: Permutation null — mean/SD/Q95/Q99/max vs observed，z-score，p-value\"\n557\t    ],\n558\t    \"figures\": [],\n559\t    \"analysis\": \"Best tier 的 critical robustness check。Null C% mean=0.21% 在 [0.0, 1.0] range 内。 z=282.6 使 temporal DIF signal 成为 unambiguous。与 random-split 的 convergence 提供 double confirmation。This goes into main text as primary robustness evidence alongside threshold sensitivity（plan_018）and decomposition（plan_019）。\\n\\n\\nPermutation null 通过 random temporal label reassignment（保持 N_ref=1080, N_foc=807） 建立 chance baseline。Mean 0.21% 与 random split 0.18% convergent，因为两者本质上 measure the same thing：无 temporal structure 时的 spurious DIF rate。0.21% vs 0.18% 微小差异来自 permutation 使用 full N=1887（random split 在 single cohort ~1000 内）。Observed 31.3% 给出 z=282.6——0/1000 permutations exceed，empirical p<0.001。这是因为 temporal structure 是 genuine signal：2023 和 2024 model cohorts 确实在 item-level functioning 上不同。 Permutation destroys this temporal structure，restoring C% to chance level (~0.2%)。 149× enrichment over null 彻底回答 \\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"。\\n\"\n560\t  },\n561\t  {\n562\t    \"name\": \"odds_ratio_regression_transparency\",\n563\t    \"description\": \"多层 logistic regression——OR + CI + McFadden/Nagelkerke R² + Simpson's paradox 展示\",\n564\t    \"results\": {\n565\t      \"model1_domain_delta\": {\n566\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0007,\n567\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0012,\n568\t        \"aic\": 15545.2,\n569\t        \"or_per_010\": 1.55,\n570\t        \"or_ci_per_010\": [\n571\t          1.19,\n572\t          2.03\n573\t        ]\n574\t      },\n575\t      \"model2_domain_plus_items\": {\n576\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0423,\n577\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.072,\n578\t        \"aic\": 14902.3,\n579\t        \"subject_delta_or_per_010\": 0.73,\n580\t        \"difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.78,\n581\t        \"discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.51\n582\t      },\n583\t      \"model3_item_delta\": {\n584\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0012,\n585\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0021,\n586\t        \"aic\": 15536.9,\n587\t        \"or\": 2.11,\n588\t        \"or_ci\": [\n589\t          1.51,\n590\t          2.96\n591\t        ]\n592\t      },\n593\t      \"model4_best\": {\n594\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0434,\n595\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0737,\n596\t        \"aic\": 14885.4,\n597\t        \"item_delta_or_per_010\": 0.92,\n598\t        \"difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.77,\n599\t        \"discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.54\n600\t      },\n601\t      \"simpsons_paradox\": true,\n602\t      \"lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2\": 646.98,\n603\t      \"lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2\": 655.53\n604\t    },\n605\t    \"tables\": [\n606\t      \"Table S17: Four-model regression summary — OR, 95% CI, R², AIC, deviance\",\n607\t      \"Table S18: Simpson's paradox — Model 1 vs Model 2 coefficient sign reversal\"\n608\t    ],\n609\t    \"figures\": [],\n610\t    \"analysis\": \"Full transparency supplement for plan_019 decomposition。Simpson's paradox 是 methodological cautionary tale：naive domain-level analysis (OR=1.55) overestimates improvement's contribution， item-level conditioning (OR=0.73) reveals the truth。Model 1 作为 primary（conservative）， Simpson's paradox 在 appendix 详述。R²=0.0007 是 \\\"≤7.6% explained\\\" claim 的 additional support。\\n\\nFour-model architecture 揭示 Simpson's paradox：accuracy improvement 的 OR 从 Model 1 的 1.55 （正相关：improved domains 有更多 DIF）reversal 到 Model 2 的 0.73（负相关：controlling for item properties 后 improvement 反而 associated with less DIF）。Paradox 成因：DIF items 更难（d=-0.247, plan_023）且 higher-discrimination（d=0.230），而这些 item properties 同时 与 accuracy change 相关（difficult domains 有 larger improvement headroom）。 Model 1 的 R²=0.0007 confirms accuracy improvement 几乎不解释 DIF variance——绝大部分 DIF 是 item-specific 而非 domain improvement 的 proxy。Model 4 R²=0.0434 shows item intrinsic properties（difficulty, discrimination）解释了 >98% 的 explainable variance。 LR test（χ²=647-656, p<0.001）confirms adding item properties 显著改善 fit。\\n\"\n611\t  }\n612\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02a66d51-3ac6-408a-bb4a-e92f7256c0c6","uuid":"6109f89b-25f6-482a-bb23-2382896927dc","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:50:27.859Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122440/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"METABENCH MMLU 5219×12508 response matrix MH-DIF 全量分析：temporal/ability cohort、within-family confound control、domain-specificity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_cohort\": {\n        \"n_ref_2023\": 1080,\n        \"n_foc_2024h1\": 807,\n        \"ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n        \"ets_b_pct\": 18.2,\n        \"ets_a_pct\": 50.5,\n        \"n_c_items\": 3918,\n        \"mean_abs_delta_mh_c_items\": 2.31\n      },\n      \"ability_cohort\": {\n        \"ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n        \"enrichment\": 1.19\n      },\n      \"within_family\": {\n        \"llama2_vs_llama3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n        \"mistral_vs_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7\n      },\n      \"domain_specificity\": {\n        \"spearman_rho_c_pct_vs_acc_delta\": 0.307,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n        \"highest_c_pct_subject\": \"moral_scenarios (48.4%)\",\n        \"lowest_c_pct_subject\": \"college_biology (20.7%)\",\n        \"unweighted_mean_c_pct\": 30.0\n      },\n      \"sanity_checks\": {\n        \"random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n        \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n      },\n      \"li_et_al_proxy\": {\n        \"coverage\": 0.738,\n        \"enrichment_temporal\": 0.96,\n        \"fpr_on_li_clean\": 0.318\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Temporal DIF summary — N_ref=1080, N_foc=807, %A/B/C by ETS class, mean |Δ_MH|\",\n      \"Table 2: 57-subject domain-specificity — per-subject C%, accuracy delta, sorted descending\",\n      \"Table S1: Within-family DIF — Llama-2v3 (N=161 vs 308), Mistral-Mixtral, C%, Jaccard with temporal\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"31.3% 是 paper 的 anchor number。Random split 0.18% 建立了 chance baseline（plan_029 permutation null 将进一步强化）。Ability cohort 的 2.9% 排除了 ability grouping 作为 confound。Domain ρ=0.307 说明 \\\"模型在某些 domain 进步更多\\\" 是 factor 之一，但不是主要因素——item-level decomposition (plan_019/030) 证明 DIF 主要是 item-specific。Within-family Llama-2→3 的 61.3% 提供了 capability evolution 的 direct evidence，同时为 plan_027 ability confound 分析铺垫。\\n\\n\\n31.3% C% 反映 genuine temporal item-level functioning changes。三层确认非伪影： (1) random split 仅 0.18%（>170x enrichment ratio 排除统计伪影）； (2) ability cohort C%=2.9%（DIF 由 temporal structure 驱动，非 ability grouping）； (3) temporal-ability Jaccard=0.014（两种 cohort 几乎 flag 完全不同的 items）。 Domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation；后续 plan_019 item-level decomposition 证明 domain improvement 仅解释 7.6%。Within-family Llama-2→3 的 61.3% 反映跨代 capability jump（d=-0.99, plan_027），而非 contamination artifact—— 同一架构族内 item functioning 剧烈变化说明 capability evolution 是 contributor 之一。 Li et al. enrichment≈0.96 在 meta-critique framing 下是 expected：web-overlap 是 model-agnostic label，DIF 检测的是 model-cohort-differential signal，二者正交。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF 对 alignment-RL 和 reasoning-RL 模型的鲁棒性验证，含 per-model detector 对比和 power analysis\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alignment_rl_cohort\": {\n        \"n_dpo_orpo_models\": 477,\n        \"temporal_c_pct_with_alignment_rl\": 30.8,\n        \"jaccard_vs_full_temporal\": 0.87,\n        \"dif_retention_ratio\": 0.94\n      },\n      \"reasoning_rl_addition\": {\n        \"n_reasoning_rl_models\": 13,\n        \"models_tested\": \"DeepSeek-R1-7B, DeepSeek-R1-32B, Qwen2.5-RL-7B/14B/32B, Eurus-RL-7B, PRIME-RL-7B, SimpleRL-7B, DAPO-7B, K1.5-RL, TinyZero-3B, DeepScaleR-1.5B, OpenChat-RL\",\n        \"temporal_c_pct_with_rl_added\": 31.1,\n        \"jaccard_vs_full_temporal\": 0.93,\n        \"c_pct_delta_from_baseline\": -0.2\n      },\n      \"per_model_detectors\": {\n        \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.71,\n        \"constat_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.67,\n        \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.43,\n        \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.64,\n        \"mink_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.59,\n        \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.37,\n        \"delong_p_constat_sft_vs_reasoning_rl\": 0.008,\n        \"delong_p_mink_sft_vs_reasoning_rl\": 0.003\n      },\n      \"power_analysis\": {\n        \"exploitation_rate_04_tpr\": 0.28,\n        \"exploitation_rate_06_tpr\": 0.47,\n        \"exploitation_rate_08_tpr\": 0.65,\n        \"exploitation_rate_10_tpr\": 0.79\n      },\n      \"tost_equivalence\": {\n        \"tost_p\": 0.034,\n        \"equivalence_margin\": 0.05,\n        \"ci_90_retention_ratio\": [\n          0.89,\n          0.98\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S2: Per-model detector AUROC — SFT vs alignment-RL vs reasoning-RL，含 bootstrap 95% CI 和 DeLong test\",\n      \"Table S3: DIF flag stability across cohort compositions — Jaccard, overlap %, new/lost flags\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Two-level validation 结论清晰：(1) group-level DIF robust to RL composition（Jaccard≥0.87）； (2) per-model detectors fragile to reasoning RL（AUROC drops 0.25-0.27 points）。 这支持 DIF 的 structural advantage 叙事但 N=13 不足以做 standalone claim。 结论：appendix + limitations，为 future work 留出空间。\\n\\n\\nAlignment RL (DPO/ORPO) 不使用 PPO clipping，NLL 分布不变，DIF 不受影响（Jaccard=0.87）。 0.87 而非 1.0 的原因是 alignment RL 模型在 borderline items 上的 response probability 略有 shift，导致少量 items 在 MH threshold 边缘翻转。13 个 reasoning-RL 模型仅占 focal cohort 1.6%， 加入后 C% 几乎不变（31.1% vs 31.3%），因为 MH 是 group-level 统计量——少量个体对 N=807 的 odds ratio 影响可忽略。传统 per-model detectors 在 reasoning-RL 上 AUROC 大幅下降（ConStat 0.71→0.43, Min-K% 0.64→0.37），因为 GRPO/PPO 训练 contracts NLL gaps（Wang et al. 机制），而 DIF 的 group-level conditioning 天然免疫此问题。但 N=13 使 TOST p=0.034 仅 marginal significant， bootstrap CI 宽（[0.89, 0.98]）。Best tier 处理：direction consistent，但诚实地在 limitations 中报告 N=13 underpowered，不作为 numbered contribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"ConStat 风格 perturbation testing——250 MMLU items 的语义等价重述 + 检测 power 评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"reformulation\": {\n        \"n_items_reformulated\": 250,\n        \"semantic_similarity_mean\": 0.92,\n        \"n_models_tested\": 50\n      },\n      \"detection\": {\n        \"constat_flagged_pct_non_rl\": 19.2,\n        \"constat_flagged_pct_all\": 17.8,\n        \"fdr_corrected_flagged_pct\": 12.3\n      },\n      \"comparison_with_dif\": {\n        \"jaccard_constat_vs_dif_c\": 0.24,\n        \"overlap_pct\": 38.2,\n        \"constat_only_pct\": 8.1,\n        \"dif_only_pct\": 22.4\n      },\n      \"power_on_semi_synthetic_gt\": {\n        \"constat_auroc\": 0.68,\n        \"dif_auroc\": 0.82\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S4: ConStat detection — flagged % by model class，含 FDR correction\",\n      \"Table S5: DIF × ConStat cross-tabulation — Jaccard, Phi, overlap\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ConStat 提供 complementary signal 但 Jaccard=0.24 说明 ensemble marginal gain 有限。 Detection mechanism 差异（temporal differential vs memorization sensitivity）使两种方法 检测近乎正交的 item 子集。此结果验证 pivot：DIF 作为 diagnostic lens 的独特价值不可被 ConStat 替代，ensemble 不如 DIF alone + robustness checks 有效。\\n\\n\\nConStat 检测 reformulation sensitivity——contaminated 模型对 verbatim 题回答正确但对 rephrased 版性能下降。19.2% 低于 DIF 31.3%，因为：(1) ConStat 仅覆盖 verbatim memorization，partial/variant contamination 不敏感；(2) MMLU 4-choice format 下 reformulation 的 accuracy drop 天然受限 （chance level 25% 提供 floor）；(3) 高质量 paraphrase 的 surface form 变化可能不足以触发 memorization-dependent 模型的 performance shift。Jaccard=0.24 confirms 两种方法检测不同 signal types——DIF 是 temporal differential functioning，ConStat 是 memorization-specific sensitivity。Semi-synthetic ground truth 上 DIF AUROC 更高（0.82 vs 0.68），因为 injected contamination 是 differential exploitation（与 DIF 检测机制对齐），而非 verbatim memorization （与 ConStat 对齐）。结论：complementary but not additive，验证了 ensemble pivot 的正确性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance 评估——12 open-weight models × 50 responses per item 的 variance-based 检测\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"setup\": {\n        \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n        \"n_responses_per_item\": 50,\n        \"temperature\": 0.8,\n        \"total_inferences\": 7512000,\n        \"gpu_hours\": 69.6\n      },\n      \"detection\": {\n        \"bimodal_items_pct\": 11.8,\n        \"high_variance_items_pct\": 15.3,\n        \"dvd_flagged_pct\": 13.2\n      },\n      \"comparison_with_dif\": {\n        \"jaccard_dvd_vs_dif_c\": 0.16,\n        \"overlap_pct\": 29.4\n      },\n      \"power\": {\n        \"dvd_auroc_verbatim_gt\": 0.61,\n        \"dvd_auroc_variant_gt\": 0.53\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S6: DVD detection — bimodal %, flagged % by model\",\n      \"Table S7: DVD vs DIF cross-tabulation\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DVD 单独使用 power 不足，且需要 ~70 GPU hours + open-weight access。 Jaccard=0.16 说明 ensemble 增益极小。结果验证了 ensemble pivot 正确性： 三种方法的 detection mechanisms 过于异质，无法有效融合。\\n\\n\\nDVD 依赖 contaminated items 产生 bimodal generation distribution（memorized answer vs random）。 11.8% bimodal 低于 DIF 31.3%，因为：(1) bimodality 仅在 extreme verbatim memorization 下出现， partial exploitation 产生 unimodal 但 shifted distribution；(2) MMLU 4-choice format 的 discrete nature 限制了 generation variance 的 discriminative range——even uncontaminated items 在 temperature sampling 下产生 high variance；(3) requires open-weight access，排除 proprietary models。Jaccard=0.16 极低，confirms DVD 和 DIF 检测几乎完全不同的 item subsets。 AUROC 对比：DVD verbatim 0.61（moderate），variant 0.53（near chance）。Variant contamination detection 接近 chance 因为 paraphrased memorization 不产生 bimodal pattern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合：majority voting + weighted fusion\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"majority_voting_2of3\": {\n        \"tpr\": 0.35,\n        \"fpr\": 0.08,\n        \"f1\": 0.38\n      },\n      \"weighted_fusion\": {\n        \"optimal_weights\": {\n          \"dif\": 0.58,\n          \"constat\": 0.27,\n          \"dvd\": 0.15\n        },\n        \"tpr\": 0.43,\n        \"fpr\": 0.09,\n        \"f1\": 0.43,\n        \"cross_val_weight_cv\": 0.34\n      },\n      \"dif_alone_reference\": {\n        \"tpr\": 0.51,\n        \"fpr\": 0.31\n      },\n      \"coverage_gain_over_dif_pp\": 4.2,\n      \"all_ensemble_fpr_below_010\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S8: Ensemble configs — 2-of-3, weighted, DIF-alone，含 95% CI\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble 核心问题是三种方法的 signal incommensurability 而非 signal complementarity。 Best tier 下此 negative result 加强了 pivot 叙事：DIF 的 diagnostic lens 价值在于其 独特的 temporal-differential perspective，不需要也不应与其他 mechanism 融合。 Goes to appendix as informative negative result。\\n\\n\\n2-of-3 majority voting TPR 仅 0.35，因为 pairwise Jaccard 0.16-0.24 导致三方法 consensus items 极少——三种方法各自检测不同 signal（temporal differential, memorization sensitivity, generation bimodality），overlap 不足以构建有效 consensus。Weighted fusion 略好（TPR=0.43） 但 cross-validation weight stability 差（CV=0.34），因为 calibration set 有限（semi-synthetic ground truth 200 items）且三种方法 error profiles 不 correlated。DIF alone TPR=0.51 高于 任何 ensemble configuration，因为 high-recall 方法被 ensemble consensus requirement 削弱。 Coverage gain 仅 +4.2pp 不 justify 额外 150 GPU hours 和 open-weight 依赖。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"GSM8K DIF 复制 + semi-synthetic 验证 + GSM1K contamination gap 相关\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_temporal_dif\": {\n        \"n_items\": 1319,\n        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n        \"n_foc\": 804,\n        \"standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n        \"external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n        \"sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n        \"standard_external_spearman\": 0.926\n      },\n      \"step2_semi_synthetic\": {\n        \"standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n        \"external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n        \"standard_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508\n      },\n      \"step3_gsm1k_correlation\": {\n        \"n_models\": 33,\n        \"pearson_r\": -0.478,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.005,\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.027,\n        \"permutation_p\": 0.014,\n        \"direction\": \"NEGATIVE — opposite to contamination hypothesis\",\n        \"leave_one_out_r_range\": [\n          -0.537,\n          -0.374\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: GSM8K temporal DIF — C% with standard/external matching, random control\",\n      \"Table S9: GSM1K correlation — Pearson/Spearman/partial r，含 leave-one-out robustness\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GSM8K 复制验证 framework portability（ΔTPR=+0.818）和 temporal DIF pattern（18.9% vs random 0.3%）。 GSM1K negative correlation 在 best tier 下 demote to appendix exploratory（N=33, CI wide）。 This result doesn't weaken any claim — it strengthens the meta-critique by empirically demonstrating DIF and contamination labels capture different signals。\\n\\n\\nGSM8K temporal C%=18.9% 低于 MMLU 31.3%，因为 GSM8K 是 single math domain（1,319 items）， item 功能相对 homogeneous，temporal change 集中在特定难度段而非 broad capability shift。 Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818 高于 MMLU 0.674，因为 GSM8K 更 unidimensional（单一 math 能力维度）， MH 的 unidimensional conditioning 更 appropriate，injection 更 cleanly detected。 GSM1K correlation r=-0.478 方向 opposite to contamination hypothesis：DIF 更多 flag 的模型 有更小的 GSM8K-GSM1K gap。这并不矛盾——DIF flags items whose difficulty changed across cohorts （78% favor 2024），而 small GSM8K-GSM1K gap 的模型恰恰是 genuine capability improvement 最强的（GSM1K 也难，real ability gains transfer）。This anti-correlation 实际上加强了 Claim 2 meta-critique：DIF 和 contamination ground truth 测量的是 different constructs。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT equating pilot——验证 MMLU 上 psychometric equating 可行性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model_fit\": {\n        \"unidimensional_rmsea\": 0.121,\n        \"unidimensional_cfi\": 0.776,\n        \"bifactor_5group_rmsea\": 0.094,\n        \"bifactor_5group_cfi\": 0.841,\n        \"bifactor_full_57_convergence\": false,\n        \"bifactor_full_57_error\": \"non-positive definite Hessian after 500 EM iterations\"\n      },\n      \"anchor_selection\": {\n        \"dif_free_items_pct\": 17.3,\n        \"n_anchors_meeting_criteria\": 2163,\n        \"anchor_icc_concordance\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"equating_attempt\": {\n        \"equated_rho\": 0.91,\n        \"target_rho\": 0.95,\n        \"shortfall\": 0.04\n      },\n      \"decision\": \"KILLED — bifactor fit insufficient (RMSEA=0.094>0.05), equated rho=0.91 < target 0.95\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S10: IRT fit comparison — unidimensional vs 5-group bifactor vs full bifactor\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Informative negative result。说明传统 psychometric equating 不能直接迁移到 LLM multi-domain benchmarks：extreme multidimensionality violates essential unidimensionality assumption。 加强 diagnostic lens framing——DIF 的价值不在于 equating-based item replacement， 而在于 understanding what changed。在 limitations 中自然 motivate future multidimensional IRT。\\n\\n\\nMMLU 57-subject 结构使 full bifactor（1 general + 57 specific）在计算上不可行—— non-positive definite Hessian 因为 57 specific factors 导致 identification 问题（many subjects 仅 100 items，insufficient for factor estimation）。Reduced 5-group bifactor 改善有限 （RMSEA 0.121→0.094, CFI 0.776→0.841），仍远低于 acceptable fit thresholds。根本原因是 MMLU 内在 multidimensionality：从 abstract_algebra 到 world_religions 的 57 domains 无法 被 1 general factor + few group factors 充分 capture。Equating pilot 在 suboptimal fit 下 仍尝试：anchors 数量足够（2,163 items），但 misspecified ability estimates 传播到 fixed-parameter calibration，导致 equated rho=0.91 低于 target 0.95。Kill decision 正确—— 此 negative result 在 limitations 中作为 future multidimensional IRT work 的 motivation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF-flagged MMLU items 的 LLM-based 替代 item 生成与难度校准\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"generation\": {\n        \"n_items_generated\": 400,\n        \"n_subjects\": 10,\n        \"construct_adherence_human_eval\": 0.784\n      },\n      \"difficulty_calibration\": {\n        \"prompt_based_rho\": 0.38,\n        \"student_sim_rho\": 0.52,\n        \"target_rho\": 0.75\n      },\n      \"quality\": {\n        \"human_quality_score_mean\": 3.2,\n        \"human_quality_target\": 4.0,\n        \"holdout_panel_rho\": 0.48\n      },\n      \"decision\": \"BELOW BENCHMARKS — best difficulty rho=0.52 vs target 0.75\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S11: Difficulty calibration — prompt vs student-sim vs empirical，含 95% CI\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"有价值的 negative result——说明 \\\"just regenerate flagged items\\\" 不是 trivial solution。 加强 diagnostic lens framing：DIF 的 actionable value 是 audit protocol + informed maintenance， 而非 automated regeneration。在 Discussion 中可用于回应 reviewer 的 \\\"so what do we do?\\\" question。\\n\\n\\nDifficulty calibration 是 item generation 的瓶颈。Prompt-based targeting（直接指定 difficulty level） rho=0.38，因为 LLM 对 \\\"difficulty for other LLMs\\\" 的 internal calibration 与 empirical difficulty 几乎无关——difficulty 由 knowledge coverage, reasoning depth, distractor quality 联合决定， 非 LLM 自身 uncertainty 可预测。Student simulation 改善到 rho=0.52，但 arXiv 2601.09953 的 r=0.75-0.82 是在 human exam items 上报告的，LLM benchmark items 的 difficulty determinants 不同（e.g., MMLU 多选的 distractor 设计对 LLM 和 human 的 difficulty contribution 不同）。 Construct fidelity 78.4% 说明 22% 的 generated items 有 subject drift 或 cognitive level 错误。 Plan_005 被 kill 后，本 plan 失去 equating framework 支撑。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Sinharay et al. (2006) cumulative Bayesian DIF priors 的 4-administration simulation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"setup\": {\n        \"n_administrations\": 4,\n        \"n_items_per_sim\": 500,\n        \"n_models_per_admin\": 200,\n        \"true_dif_items\": 100,\n        \"delta_range\": [\n          0.8,\n          1.8\n        ]\n      },\n      \"power_accumulation\": {\n        \"tpr_admin1_d10\": 0.41,\n        \"tpr_admin2_d10\": 0.58,\n        \"tpr_admin3_d10\": 0.72,\n        \"tpr_admin4_d10\": 0.81,\n        \"tpr_admin1_d08\": 0.22,\n        \"tpr_admin2_d08\": 0.38,\n        \"tpr_admin3_d08\": 0.53,\n        \"tpr_admin4_d08\": 0.65\n      },\n      \"fpr_stability\": {\n        \"fpr_range\": [\n          0.042,\n          0.045\n        ]\n      },\n      \"bayesian_shrinkage\": {\n        \"posterior_sd_admin4\": 0.31\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S12: Cumulative power — TPR at δ=0.8/1.0/1.4/1.8 × 1-4 administrations\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Clean simulation 支持 audit protocol 的 operational recommendation：每 6 月 DIF assessment， 3 次累积后 medium effects 的 power 从 0.41 升至 0.72。Goes to appendix，在 Discussion 中 referenced。\\n\\n\\nBayesian evidence accumulation 的 power gain 等价于 effectively increasing sample precision。 δ=1.0 时单次 TPR=0.41（与 phase2 sim 的 N=80 结果一致），4 次累积达 0.81——posterior SD 从 1.0 shrink 到 0.31，precision quadruples。对 small effects（δ=0.8），MH 单次几乎无法检测 （TPR=0.22），但 4 次累积达 0.65——这是 monitoring protocol 的核心理论支撑。 FPR 稳定在 ~0.043 因为 Bayesian shrinkage 对 null items 同样有效（posterior for null items 集中在 0 附近）。Simulation-only 但为 audit protocol 的 monitoring frequency 建议提供 quantitative basis。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Benchmark validity 在 progressive item removal 下的降级分析\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"progressive_removal\": {\n        \"pct_5\": {\n          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9998,\n          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.993,\n          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.98\n        },\n        \"pct_10\": {\n          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9994,\n          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.991,\n          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.96\n        },\n        \"pct_20\": {\n          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9987,\n          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.987,\n          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.92\n        },\n        \"pct_31\": {\n          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9965,\n          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.982,\n          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.87\n        },\n        \"pct_50\": {\n          \"ranking_rho\": 0.9912,\n          \"reliability_alpha\": 0.971,\n          \"construct_jaccard\": 0.78\n        }\n      },\n      \"theoretical_match\": {\n        \"spearman_brown_predicted_rho_31pct\": 0.9968,\n        \"empirical_rho_31pct\": 0.9965,\n        \"gap\": 0.0003\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S13: Progressive degradation — rho, reliability, coverage at 5/10/20/31/50%\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"直接支持 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" 叙事。31% instability 不威胁 validity（rho=0.997） 因为 MMLU 的 massive redundancy。Headline number 进 main text，full curve 进 appendix。\\n\\n\\nMMLU 12,508 items 的 massive redundancy 决定了 removal 的 graceful degradation。 Spearman-Brown formula 预测 test length 缩减 31% 时 rho 从 ~1.0 降至 0.9968—— empirical 0.9965 精确匹配，说明 degradation 完全由 test shortening 驱动，无 systematic bias（DIF items 不是 systematically more informative for ranking）。Construct coverage 降速快于 ranking stability，因为 DIF items 在 domains 间非均匀分布（moral_scenarios 48.4% vs college_biology 20.7%），high-DIF domains 在 removal 后 coverage 受损更大。 与 plan_017 实际结果（rho=0.997 at 31%）高度一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"Item-Focused Trees（Tutz & Berger 2016）——连续时间 DIF 作为 MH categorical split 的 robustness check\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"detection\": {\n        \"ift_flagged_pct\": 28.7,\n        \"jaccard_ift_vs_mh_c\": 0.78,\n        \"ift_only_pct\": 4.2,\n        \"mh_only_pct\": 6.8\n      },\n      \"temporal_patterns\": {\n        \"single_changepoint_pct\": 71,\n        \"multiple_changepoints_pct\": 12,\n        \"gradual_drift_pct\": 17,\n        \"median_changepoint\": \"2023-09\"\n      },\n      \"tree_structure\": {\n        \"mean_terminal_nodes\": 5.2,\n        \"max_depth\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S14: IFT vs MH concordance — Jaccard, overlap, unique flags\",\n      \"Table S15: Changepoint timing distribution by quarter\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confirms MH categorical split robustness（Jaccard=0.78）。Changepoint timing 提供 temporal granularity，在 Discussion 中简要引用。Appendix robustness check。\\n\\n\\nIFT 用 continuous release date 替代 MH 的 binary temporal split，避免 arbitrary cutoff。 28.7% vs MH 31.3% 的差异来自 tree-based multiple testing correction（node-level significance threshold）vs MH 的 per-item testing。Jaccard=0.78 高一致性说明 MH categorical split captures the main temporal signal。IFT 的独特 value 是 changepoint timing：71% items 有 single changepoint（median 2023-09，对应 Llama-2/Mistral/Phi-1 release 密集期）， 12% 有 multiple changepoints（progressive drift），17% gradual drift。Timing information 支持 Discussion 中的 \\\"what drives instability\\\" narrative——major model releases 是 item functioning change 的 primary driver。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Architecture-homogeneous subpopulation DIF——验证 architecture heterogeneity 非 confound\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"metabench_composition\": {\n        \"total_models\": 5227,\n        \"decoder_only\": 5226,\n        \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n        \"non_decoder\": 1,\n        \"non_decoder_id\": \"flan-ul2\"\n      },\n      \"dif_comparison\": {\n        \"decoder_only_c_pct\": 31.3,\n        \"full_c_pct\": 31.3,\n        \"jaccard\": 1.0,\n        \"items_changed\": 0\n      },\n      \"irt_fit\": {\n        \"full_rmsea\": 0.121,\n        \"decoder_only_rmsea\": 0.121,\n        \"delta_rmsea\": 0.0\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S16: Architecture composition\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"One-line main text defense。IRT misfit 重定向至 limitations（multidimensionality motivation）。\\n\\n\\nMETABENCH MMLU 的 architecture homogeneity 使本实验成为 trivial pass：99.98% decoder-only， 唯一的 encoder-decoder (flan-ul2) 在 N=5227 中的影响可忽略。Jaccard=1.0 意味着 zero items 的 DIF classification 因 architecture stratification 而改变。IRT fit 同样不变 （RMSEA=0.121），因为 misfit 源自 57-subject multidimensionality 而非 architecture heterogeneity。 这是 ideal robustness result：potential confound 被 data composition 自然消除。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Known contamination injection 进 real response matrix + DIF detection power 评估 + cross-subject matching 验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_external_matching\": {\n        \"baseline_fpr\": 0.314,\n        \"tpr_p00\": 0.326,\n        \"tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n        \"tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n        \"tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n        \"tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n        \"delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674\n      },\n      \"ability_external_matching\": {\n        \"baseline_fpr\": 0.493,\n        \"tpr_p10\": 0.8,\n        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302\n      },\n      \"matching_variable_contamination\": {\n        \"standard_fpr_p10\": 0.616,\n        \"standard_fpr_baseline\": 0.298,\n        \"fpr_inflation\": 0.318,\n        \"cross_subject_fpr_inflation\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"cross_subject_5subj_validation\": {\n        \"delta_fpr_all_subjects\": 0.0,\n        \"avg_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n        \"subjects_passing_p05\": \"4/5\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: Semi-synthetic ΔTPR/ΔFPR across exploitation rates and matching strategies\",\n      \"Table 6: Standard vs cross-subject matching FPR comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ΔTPR=+0.508 是 Claim 3 headline。Cross-subject ΔFPR=0.000 是 key methodological novelty。 Dose-response pattern 提供 internal validity。Both metrics 在 best tier range 内。\\n\\n\\nSemi-synthetic injection 在 real response matrix 上创造 controlled ground truth—— 对 focal cohort 的 known-clean items 执行 incorrect→correct flipping with probability p。 ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 在 best tier [0.45, 0.55] range 内，confirms DIF detects moderate differential contamination。Dose-response（p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0 对应 TPR 0.55→0.83→0.99→1.0） 增强因果推断。关键 methodological finding：standard MH matching（total score 含 contaminated items） 导致 FPR inflation +0.318（matching variable contamination），而 cross-subject matching （other subjects 的 total score）完全消除 inflation（ΔFPR=0.000）。Cross-subject matching works 因为 contamination 是 subject-specific（inject 进特定 subject），而 other subjects 的 total score 不受 contamination 影响，保持 conditioning variable 的 exchangeability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"6 benchmarks temporal DIF——cross-benchmark generalizability 验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu\": {\n        \"n_items\": 12508,\n        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n        \"n_foc\": 807,\n        \"pct_c\": 31.3,\n        \"random_pct_c\": 0.18\n      },\n      \"winogrande\": {\n        \"n_items\": 1267,\n        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n        \"n_foc\": 803,\n        \"pct_c\": 30.3,\n        \"random_pct_c\": 0.32\n      },\n      \"truthfulqa\": {\n        \"n_items\": 817,\n        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n        \"n_foc\": 807,\n        \"pct_c\": 29.7,\n        \"random_pct_c\": 0.37\n      },\n      \"arc\": {\n        \"n_items\": 1172,\n        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n        \"n_foc\": 807,\n        \"pct_c\": 26.9,\n        \"random_pct_c\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"gsm8k\": {\n        \"n_items\": 1319,\n        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n        \"n_foc\": 804,\n        \"pct_c\": 18.9,\n        \"random_pct_c\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"hellaswag\": {\n        \"n_items\": 10042,\n        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n        \"n_foc\": 807,\n        \"pct_c\": 17.9,\n        \"random_pct_c\": 0.28\n      },\n      \"summary\": {\n        \"range\": \"17.9–31.3%\",\n        \"all_random_below_1pct\": true,\n        \"min_enrichment_ratio\": 44.8,\n        \"mean_c_pct\": 25.8,\n        \"n_benchmarks\": 6\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: Cross-benchmark temporal DIF — 6 rows, N_items/N_ref/N_foc/C%/random%\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark consistency 是 Claim 1 generalizability 最强证据。17.9-31.3% range 在 best tier [17.0, 32.0] 内。Claim 1 statement 可升级为 \\\"17.9-31.3% across 6 major benchmarks\\\"。\\n\\n\\n6 benchmarks 一致显示 temporal DIF 远超 chance（enrichment 45-174×），确认 temporal item instability 是 LLM benchmark 的 general phenomenon。C% ordering 反映 benchmark 结构： MMLU（57 domains, maximal multidimensionality）和 WinoGrande（commonsense reasoning, capability-sensitive） 最高；HellaSwag（sentence completion, more pattern-matching than reasoning）和 GSM8K （single math domain）最低。低 C% benchmarks 的 items 功能更 homogeneous across model generations ——sentence completion patterns evolve less than knowledge/reasoning items。 All random controls <1% 排除 statistical artifact across all benchmarks。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"permutation_null_c_rate\",\n    \"description\": \"1000× permutation test——temporal label shuffling 下的 C% null distribution\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"null_distribution\": {\n        \"n_permutations\": 1000,\n        \"mean_c_pct\": 0.21,\n        \"sd_c_pct\": 0.11,\n        \"median_c_pct\": 0.19,\n        \"q95_c_pct\": 0.42,\n        \"q99_c_pct\": 0.54,\n        \"max_c_pct\": 0.71\n      },\n      \"significance\": {\n        \"observed_c_pct\": 31.3,\n        \"z_score\": 282.6,\n        \"empirical_p\": \"<0.001 (0/1000 exceed observed)\",\n        \"ratio_observed_to_null_mean\": 149\n      },\n      \"consistency\": {\n        \"random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n        \"permutation_null_mean\": 0.21,\n        \"convergent\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7: Permutation null — mean/SD/Q95/Q99/max vs observed，z-score，p-value\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Best tier 的 critical robustness check。Null C% mean=0.21% 在 [0.0, 1.0] range 内。 z=282.6 使 temporal DIF signal 成为 unambiguous。与 random-split 的 convergence 提供 double confirmation。This goes into main text as primary robustness evidence alongside threshold sensitivity（plan_018）and decomposition（plan_019）。\\n\\n\\nPermutation null 通过 random temporal label reassignment（保持 N_ref=1080, N_foc=807） 建立 chance baseline。Mean 0.21% 与 random split 0.18% convergent，因为两者本质上 measure the same thing：无 temporal structure 时的 spurious DIF rate。0.21% vs 0.18% 微小差异来自 permutation 使用 full N=1887（random split 在 single cohort ~1000 内）。Observed 31.3% 给出 z=282.6——0/1000 permutations exceed，empirical p<0.001。这是因为 temporal structure 是 genuine signal：2023 和 2024 model cohorts 确实在 item-level functioning 上不同。 Permutation destroys this temporal structure，restoring C% to chance level (~0.2%)。 149× enrichment over null 彻底回答 \\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"odds_ratio_regression_transparency\",\n    \"description\": \"多层 logistic regression——OR + CI + McFadden/Nagelkerke R² + Simpson's paradox 展示\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model1_domain_delta\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0007,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0012,\n        \"aic\": 15545.2,\n        \"or_per_010\": 1.55,\n        \"or_ci_per_010\": [\n          1.19,\n          2.03\n        ]\n      },\n      \"model2_domain_plus_items\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0423,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.072,\n        \"aic\": 14902.3,\n        \"subject_delta_or_per_010\": 0.73,\n        \"difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.78,\n        \"discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.51\n      },\n      \"model3_item_delta\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0012,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0021,\n        \"aic\": 15536.9,\n        \"or\": 2.11,\n        \"or_ci\": [\n          1.51,\n          2.96\n        ]\n      },\n      \"model4_best\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0434,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0737,\n        \"aic\": 14885.4,\n        \"item_delta_or_per_010\": 0.92,\n        \"difficulty_or_per_010\": 0.77,\n        \"discrimination_or_per_010\": 1.54\n      },\n      \"simpsons_paradox\": true,\n      \"lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2\": 646.98,\n      \"lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2\": 655.53\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S17: Four-model regression summary — OR, 95% CI, R², AIC, deviance\",\n      \"Table S18: Simpson's paradox — Model 1 vs Model 2 coefficient sign reversal\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Full transparency supplement for plan_019 decomposition。Simpson's paradox 是 methodological cautionary tale：naive domain-level analysis (OR=1.55) overestimates improvement's contribution， item-level conditioning (OR=0.73) reveals the truth。Model 1 作为 primary（conservative）， Simpson's paradox 在 appendix 详述。R²=0.0007 是 \\\"≤7.6% explained\\\" claim 的 additional support。\\n\\nFour-model architecture 揭示 Simpson's paradox：accuracy improvement 的 OR 从 Model 1 的 1.55 （正相关：improved domains 有更多 DIF）reversal 到 Model 2 的 0.73（负相关：controlling for item properties 后 improvement 反而 associated with less DIF）。Paradox 成因：DIF items 更难（d=-0.247, plan_023）且 higher-discrimination（d=0.230），而这些 item properties 同时 与 accuracy change 相关（difficult domains 有 larger improvement headroom）。 Model 1 的 R²=0.0007 confirms accuracy improvement 几乎不解释 DIF variance——绝大部分 DIF 是 item-specific 而非 domain improvement 的 proxy。Model 4 R²=0.0434 shows item intrinsic properties（difficulty, discrimination）解释了 >98% 的 explainable variance。 LR test（χ²=647-656, p<0.001）confirms adding item properties 显著改善 fit。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":612,"startLine":1,"totalLines":612}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Aa1m7pALuaHtSorMP3rHhv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me also read the paper writing norms skill since this is a paper writing task.\n\nLet me now draft the complete LaTeX paper. I need to:\n\n1. Structure: Abstract, Introduction, Related Work, Method, Experiments, Discussion/Conclusion, Limitations\n2. Cover all experiments from experiment_data.json\n3. Follow EMNLP 2026 8-page limit (this is a dream paper so it should be approximately this length)\n4. Follow the narrative guidance and paper_framing.md\n\nLet me organize the experiments:\n\n**Main body experiments:**\n- real_data_dif_mmlu (Claim 1 - Table 1, 2)\n\n\n- multi_benchmark_temporal_dif (Claim 1 generalizability - Table 3)\n- semi_synthetic_contamination_validation (Claim 3 - Table 5, 6)\n- cross_benchmark_gsm8k (Claim 3 cross-benchmark + Claim 1 GSM8K - Table 4)\n- permutation_null_c_rate (Robustness - Table 7)\n- graceful_degradation_analysis (Claim 4 - in main text)\n- odds_ratio_regression_transparency (Claim 1 decomposition - appendix but referenced)\n\n**Appendix experiments:**\n- rl_robustness_validation and remaining experiments covering perturbation evaluation, generation variance, ensemble fusion, IRT equating, item calibration, Bayesian DIF, tree-based analysis, and architecture stratification across supplementary tables\n\nNow I'm mapping out the paper structure and table assignments. I'll organize the main results around temporal DIF patterns across benchmarks, domain specificity findings, cross-benchmark validation, and robustness checks, then move into the appendix experiments that support each claim.\n\nI'm ready to draft the full LaTeX document with comprehensive sections covering the methodology, results, and implications while keeping the main text to around 8 pages.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the key quantitative findings to weave throughout: the permutation null establishing statistical significance at z=282.6, the semi-synthetic validation showing a dose-response effect with substantial true positive rate gains, cross-subject matching confirming no false positive inflation, and the ranking stability remaining remarkably high even after removing a third of the data. I'm also noting the circularity ablation results that strongly favor the DIF-based approach, the architectural homogeneity across models, threshold sensitivity patterns, and the enrichment validation against existing web-overlap labels.\n\nThe robustness checks show the RL framework remains stable with high Jaccard overlap, though IFT shows somewhat lower agreement with the Mokken-Hemker approach, and the IRT misfit metrics suggest some multidimensionality that I'll need to address as a limitation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14355,"cache_read_input_tokens":24214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14355},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02a66d51-3ac6-408a-bb4a-e92f7256c0c6","uuid":"75b27ede-662f-4b29-888e-41330a82c221"}
